From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-lenovo-tb320fc: adapt the board
 file to the kShim handoff

The XBL loader populates the DDR map in the runtime (Android) DTB and
kShim rebuilds the payload memory node from it, so the placeholder
needs no patching.  The Gen2 board has no fixed splash or ramoops
reservation in the saved DTB, so there is nothing to disable.

Detach the DPU from the application SMMU and drop the inert
qcom,preserve-boot-mappings property: mainline has no SM8475 boot-
mapping handoff, and the DPU runs identity-mapped like the sm8450
board file.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-tb320fc.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-tb320fc.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-tb320fc.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-tb320fc.dts
@@ -448,7 +448,13 @@
 };
 
 &mdss_mdp {
-	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x800 0x2>;
+	/*
+	 * kShim handoff: run the DPU without the application SMMU, like the
+	 * upstream sm8450 board file.  The vendor tree attaches SID 0x800, but
+	 * mainline has no SM8475 boot-mapping handoff (the elden patch only
+	 * covers the SM8750 DPU), so v1 uses identity mapping.
+	 */
+	/delete-property/ iommus;
 };
 
 &mdss_dsi0 {
@@ -598,7 +604,7 @@
 };
 
 &apps_smmu {
-	qcom,preserve-boot-mappings;
+	/* No mainline consumer on SM8475; the property is dropped here. */
 };
 
 &tlmm {
-- 
